### Works with the IntelliJ / VS Code REST client. Base URL and users: see README.
@host = http://localhost:8080
@eng = Basic ZW5naW5lZXI6ZW5naW5lZXIxMjM=
@apr = Basic YXBwcm92ZXI6YXBwcm92ZXIxMjM=

### Health
GET {{host}}/api/v1/health

### Create a short URL
POST {{host}}/api/v1/urls
Authorization: {{eng}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "originalUrl": "https://example.com/articles/spring-boot", "customAlias": "spring-guide", "expirationDate": "2027-01-01T00:00:00" }

### Redirect (302)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/urls/spring-guide
Referer: https://news.example.org/post

### Analytics
GET {{host}}/api/v1/urls/spring-guide/analytics
Authorization: {{eng}}

### Create a workflow (scenario 1)
# @name wf
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workflows
Authorization: {{eng}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requirement": "Build a URL shortener that supports custom aliases, expiration, redirects, and click analytics." }

### Execute
@id = {{wf.response.body.$.id}}
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workflows/{{id}}/execute
Authorization: {{eng}}

### Tasks / DAG
GET {{host}}/api/v1/workflows/{{id}}/tasks
Authorization: {{eng}}

### Approve (APPROVER)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workflows/{{id}}/approve
Authorization: {{apr}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "approved" }

### Summary and metrics
GET {{host}}/api/v1/workflows/{{id}}/summary
Authorization: {{eng}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/metrics/summary
Authorization: {{eng}}